*  ============================================================================
*  PB-1s PER-SITE SNAPSHOT CELL -- root cause verified s107 (Claude Opus 5).
*  A pattern-valued statement that needs an MKPAT blob (an ALT is enough) has
*  every plain variable reference snapshotted into a hidden global named per
*  LOWERING SITE: "PAT$<blob>$V<i>" (lower_snobol4.c:2222 and :2504, "%s$V%d").
*  The built pattern DEFER-reads that global BY NAME at match time.
*  Manual p.85-86: each construction freezes ITS OWN values at construction
*  time ("NPAT captures the value of variable N at the time of pattern
*  construction"); only unary * defers.  One cell per SITE cannot do that.
*  Oracle: /home/claude/x64/bin/sbl -b <file>
*  ============================================================================
*  RED -- SIG11 both modes (m3 == m4).  Self-referential accumulation at ONE site,
*  executed TWICE.  Iteration 2 stores into PAT$1$V0 a pattern that ITSELF defers to
*  PAT$1$V0 => cyclic structure => unbounded match recursion (~67MB stack) => SIG11.
*  NOTE: contains NO variable reference in the ALT -- pure literals.  This FALSIFIES
*  the s106 label "an ALT arm holding a snapshot-deferred plain ref": the plain ref is
*  not an ingredient.  The ingredients are (1) an ALT (forces the MKPAT blob route),
*  (2) SELF-REFERENCE of the assignment target, (3) the SAME site run twice.
*
*  ⭐ THIS IS THE MINIMAL FORM OF beauty_suite/case_driver (Milestone 1 blocker).
*  case.sno:23 is this shape verbatim:
*        icase = icase (upr(letter) | lwr(letter))      :(icase)
*  self-reference + ALT + goto loop back to the SAME site.  FINGERPRINT MATCH: both
*  this witness and case_driver.sno die at rsp=0x7ffffbffeff0 with an unwalkable
*  backtrace (~67MB of stack consumed) -- the same exhaustion depth to the byte.
*  ⛔ The upr()/lwr() CALLS IN THE ARMS ARE INCIDENTAL.  s98 / s105 / s106 each
*  labelled case_driver an "eager call" defect; three sessions chased the calls.
*  This witness crashes with pure literals and no call anywhere.
        mk = LEN(0)
        n = 0
LP      n = n + 1
        mk = mk ('X' | 'y')
        LT(n,2)                         :S(LP)
        'Xy' mk                         :F(NO)
        OUTPUT = 'MATCHED cycle'        :(FIN)
NO      OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH cycle'
FIN
END
